---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const updated = 'August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Refunds · Warren Labs"
  description="Fourteen days, no questions asked. How to request a refund on Warren Labs audio software, what happens to your licence, and what to do if we don't reply."
>
  <Nav variant="home" />
  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Refunds</span>
      <h2>Refund Policy</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        <b>14 days, no questions asked.</b> Email
        <a href="mailto:jamey@warrenlabs.com?subject=Refund%20request">jamey@warrenlabs.com</a>
        with your order number and we'll refund it. You don't have to explain why, and we won't ask
        you to sit through an attempt to talk you out of it.
      </p>

      <h3>Why no questions</h3>
      <p>
        You cannot properly evaluate a mixing tool in a shop. You have to put it on a real session,
        on your own material, in your own room, and find out whether it earns its place. That takes
        more than a demo and it sometimes ends in no. A refund policy that makes you argue your case
        is a policy designed to keep money from people who found out the honest way.
      </p>

      <h3>How to ask</h3>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:jamey@warrenlabs.com?subject=Refund%20request">jamey@warrenlabs.com</a>
        with the order number from your receipt, within 14 days of purchase. That's the whole
        process. You'll get a reply from a person, usually the same day.
      </p>

      <h3>What happens next</h3>
      <p>
        <b>FastSpring is the merchant of record</b> — the legal seller — so the money goes back the
        way it came, through them, to the card or account you paid with. We authorise it; they move
        it. Expect the refund to appear within a few business days, depending on your bank, and the
        line on your statement will name FastSpring rather than Warren Labs.
      </p>

      <h3>What happens to your licence</h3>
      <p>
        It stops being valid, and we'll say plainly what that does and doesn't mean. Your
        <code>.wllicense</code> file verifies offline, so a copy sitting on a machine that never
        goes online is not something we can reach out and switch off. We're asking you to delete it
        and stop using the software, and we're trusting you to.
      </p>
      <p>
        We'd rather tell you the truth about how the licensing works than imply a remote kill switch
        we deliberately chose not to build. The same design that means we can't revoke your licence
        is the one that means our servers going away can't revoke it either.
      </p>

      <h3>If we don't reply</h3>
      <p>
        We should, and quickly. But if you email a refund request and hear nothing for
        <b>two business days</b>, you can take it straight to
        <a href="https://fastspring.com/consumer-support/" rel="noopener">FastSpring's support</a>
        and they will handle it. That's their policy as merchant of record, and we're telling you
        about it up front rather than leaving you to discover it while frustrated.
      </p>

      <h3>After 14 days</h3>
      <p>
        Write to us anyway. The 14 days is a promise, not a shutter — it's the window where the
        answer is automatically yes. Past it, if the software isn't doing what we said it does, or
        something went wrong on our side, we'd still rather sort it out than hold you to a date.
      </p>

      <h3>Your statutory rights</h3>
      <p>
        If you're a consumer in the EU or the UK, you have a statutory right of withdrawal for
        online purchases, and nothing on this page reduces it. Where those rights give you more than
        this policy does, they win. This policy is written to sit at or above that floor, so you
        shouldn't ever need to work out which applies.
      </p>

      <h3>Chargebacks</h3>
      <p>
        Please email first. A chargeback costs us a fee on top of the refund and takes months to
        resolve, and there is genuinely no scenario where it gets you your money faster than just
        asking. If you've already filed one, tell us and we'll stop duplicating the work.
      </p>

      <h3>Contact</h3>
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:jamey@warrenlabs.com">jamey@warrenlabs.com</a>. Include the order number if
        you have it; we'll find it if you don't.
      </p>

      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Footer variant="home" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 720px; }
  .prose h3 { margin: 30px 0 8px; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .prose p { margin: 0 0 14px; line-height: 1.65; }
  .prose code { font-size: 0.92em; }
  .prose .updated { margin-top: 30px; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.55; }
</style>
